//? Title: Empirical likelihood for a mean
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en

The ordinary sample mean gives equal probability to each observation.
Empirical likelihood fits probabilities subject to a specified mean and
compares their product with the product under equal probabilities. Inverting
that likelihood-ratio test gives an asymptotic confidence interval.

```{cpp, id=empirical-mean, cache=yes, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <datamunge/stats/robust_summary.hpp>
#include <print>
#include <vector>

int main() {
    using namespace datamunge::stats;
    const std::vector<double> sample{1, 1, 4, 5, 9};
    const auto fit = empirical_likelihood_mean_test(sample, 6);
    const auto ci = empirical_likelihood_mean_interval(sample);
    std::println("| Observation | Weight when the mean is 6 |");
    std::println("| ---: | ---: |");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < sample.size(); ++i)
        std::println("| {:.0f} | {:.4f} |", sample[i], fit.weights[i]);
    std::println("\nThe likelihood-ratio statistic is {:.3f}, with p = {:.3f}.", fit.statistic, fit.p_value);
    std::println("The sample mean is {:.1f}. Its empirical likelihood interval is [{:.3f}, {:.3f}].",
                 ci.estimate, ci.lower, ci.upper);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| Observation | Weight when the mean is 6 |
| ---: | ---: |
| 1 | 0.1009 |
| 1 | 0.1009 |
| 4 | 0.1436 |
| 5 | 0.1671 |
| 9 | 0.4876 |

The likelihood-ratio statistic is 1.978, with p = 0.160.
The sample mean is 4.0. Its empirical likelihood interval is [1.924, 6.761].
